3. USE

The Library's functionality ("Smart Cleanup") is a paid Cloudless
product. It includes a free monthly allowance, metered by the Library;
beyond that allowance it requires an active, paid Cloudless subscription.
All use of Smart Cleanup is subject to the Subscription Terms. This applies
equally to the official Cloudless Voice application and to any Fork: a Fork
may offer Smart Cleanup to its users, provided each user uses their own
Cloudless account and complies with the Subscription Terms.
You may build and run Cloudless Voice or a Fork that contains the Library
without a paid subscription; once the free allowance is used up, the
Library will not perform Smart Cleanup until a user with an active
subscription signs in. Builds that are not signed with an Apple Developer
team receive no free allowance. Dictation itself does not depend on the
Library.

You must not circumvent, disable or interfere with the usage metering, the
subscription check or any other license enforcement in the Library or in
the code that calls it, or provide Smart Cleanup beyond the free allowance
to anyone who does not hold an active Cloudless subscription.

